@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #526B7B
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #EDF4FB
skinparam activityBorderColor #526B7B
skinparam activityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3DF
skinparam activityDiamondBorderColor #B99557
skinparam activityStartColor #163E52
skinparam activityEndColor #163E52
skinparam wrapWidth 190
skinparam maxMessageSize 180

title CF-M16 — Conditional isolated restore and usability assessment
start
:CF-M16-S01\nInitiating actor\nOperator identifies a\nloss/recovery scenario and\nrequests an explicitly authorized\nisolated drill.;
if (CF-M16-S02\nAuthorized isolated target,\nidentified protected source and\nrequired recovery coverage\nactually exist?) then (yes)
:CF-M16-S03\nOperator\nDefine covered scenario, required\nmaterial, criteria and measurement\ncontext;
:CF-M16-S04\nSystem / Operator\nPerform only explicitly authorized\nisolated restoration;
if (CF-M16-S05\nActual restored candidate\navailable?) then (yes)
:CF-M16-S06\nOperator / System\nCheck integrity, required data,\ncurrent access and external-state\ndisposition;
:CF-M16-S07\nOperator\nMeasure actual recovery result\nagainst defined targets;
if (CF-M16-S08\nRequired scoped usability/targets\ndemonstrated?) then (yes)
:CF-M16-S09\nSystem\nRecord scoped usable recovery\nevidence; retain limits and\nmeasurements;
stop
else (no)
:CF-M16-S10\nSystem\nRecord incomplete/failed\nassessment and actual gaps; no\nblanket recovery claim;
stop
endif
else (no)
if (CF-M16-S11\nDefinite restore failure\nestablished?) then (yes)
:CF-M16-S12\nSystem\nRecord failed/incomplete recovery\nevidence;
stop
else (no)
:CF-M16-S13\nSystem\nRestore result unknown; reconcile\nactual isolated candidate before\nnext action;
stop
endif
endif
else (no)
:CF-M16-S14\nSystem\nDeny before prohibited effect or\nprotected disclosure; report unmet\ngate;
stop
endif
legend bottom
A: accepted profile core only. Other policy detail: P / proposed refinement.
Step IDs identify full descriptions in the activity view.
Logical ordering; no atomicity, runtime, timing or execution proof.
endlegend
@enduml
